# Per-tool global concordance

**What this is.** For each comparison tool (FLARE / Rye / RF as
available) we compute popout-vs-tool Pearson r and CCC per
(cluster, RF label) and aggregate across clusters. The chart shows
the CCC distribution per RF label as a boxplot (n_clusters > 5)
or strip plot otherwise. The table per tool carries the cohort
roll-up sourced from `cohort_summary.json:pairs[]`.

**How to read this chart.** Each box covers one RF label; the line
through it is the median across clusters. The green dashed line
at 0.90 is the CCC pass threshold; the red dashed line at 0.50 is
the rough "this label is broken for this tool" warning. Long
boxes that straddle both lines mean some clusters pass cleanly
and others fail badly — a sign that the label's reliability is
cluster-specific, not cohort-wide.

